Protocol version 2026-07-28 aligns the resource-not-found condition with
JSON-RPC by reporting InvalidParams (-32602) instead of the MCP-specific
-32002. The code is chosen per request, so a client using an earlier revision
still sees the code its revision specifies, even on a long-lived session that
has already served a modern request. Both carry the URI in the error's data,
as the specification's examples do.

-- client --
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "resources/read",
  "params": {
    "uri": "file:///missing",
    "_meta": {
      "io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion": "2026-07-28",
      "io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities": {}
    }
  }
}
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "resources/read",
  "params": { "uri": "file:///missing" }
}
-- server --
{
	"error": {
		"code": -32602,
		"data": {
			"uri": "file:///missing"
		},
		"message": "handler not found for resource URI 'file:///missing': resource not found"
	},
	"id": 1,
	"jsonrpc": "2.0"
}

{
	"error": {
		"code": -32002,
		"data": {
			"uri": "file:///missing"
		},
		"message": "handler not found for resource URI 'file:///missing': resource not found"
	},
	"id": 2,
	"jsonrpc": "2.0"
}
